Subject: [PATCH] checkpoint(jcat): snapshot of the interrupted round-2 fix at
 the stop order (unverified, incomplete)

The simplification study (09_APPROX_STUDY) was stopped by directive on
2026-11-11 while the workflow that applies the second-round review findings
was running. This commit records the working tree exactly as it was at the
stop, so that nothing is lost:

- stage a1 (reference definitions, exact time rule, validity rules):
  finished by its agent; self-reported only, not independently verified
- stage b2 (approximation-study measurements): finished by its agent;
  self-reported only, not independently verified
- stage a2 (membership / mechanism evidence, engine refactor):
  interrupted before it reported
- stage b3 (ledger inputs), the adversarial verify/fix loop and the
  regeneration of measurements, records and reports: not started

No test or benchmark was run after the stop (the files were only parsed
statically). The measurement files, records and reports in this tree still
correspond to the code of 43ba5d7, not to the code in this commit. The next
commit restores the code to that last consistent state; this commit keeps
the interrupted edits in history.

